        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: work order identified; event-level conclusion remains unverified\n\nThe September manufacturing order ending in **1070** is **MO-25-09-1070**, work order **WO-2025-09-004**, for a **Cooler Plate Pack** at Modine’s Racine operation.\n\n| Requested item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Work order | **WO-2025-09-004 / MO-25-09-1070** |\n| September cost period | **PER-COST-2025-09 — Sep-25** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Source transaction | Not available in the accessible records |\n| Event amount | Not available |\n| Exact event-created time | Not available |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Not available |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | Cannot determine without the event’s type, creation time, and recorded status |\n\nThe accessible records contain work orders and cost periods, but **no cost-event rows**. Access to the supporting records was denied. This does **not** establish that no late event occurred; it means the event-level evidence is unavailable for verification. The source timestamp above does not specify a timezone.\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nOracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B states that newly created transactions falling in or before a period in **Pending Close** are not staged in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting; they are processed after the period is closed or reopened. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** that continue processing.\n\n*Source: “Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” PDF page 233, printed page 225.*\n\nAccordingly, an ordinary newly created transaction processed while the period remained Pending Close would be inconsistent with that treatment, but the exceptions must be checked before reaching a conclusion.\n\nI requested an authorized event extract and saved the partial audit report. **No database records were changed.**",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
